# XSH putchar()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.putchar.001
anchor     functions/putchar.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fputc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       With standard output on a new file, putchar('h') returns 'h' with
           ftell(stdout) then 1, putchar('i') returns 'i' with ftell(stdout)
           then 2, and after fflush(stdout) the file holds "hi".
test       t/001-writes.c

assertion  XSH.putchar.002
anchor     functions/putchar.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fputc.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fputc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       With standard output on a new file, putchar(0x141) returns 0x41,
           putchar(-1) returns 0xff and putchar(0x100) returns 0, and after
           fflush(stdout) the file holds the bytes 0x41, 0xff, 0x00.
test       t/002-converted.c

assertion  XSH.putchar.003
anchor     functions/putchar.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       With standard output on a new file, putc('a', stdout),
           putchar('b'), putc('c', stdout) and putchar('d') return their
           arguments, ftell(stdout) is then 4, and after fflush(stdout) the
           file holds "abcd".
test       t/003-same-as-putc.c

assertion  XSH.putchar.004
anchor     functions/putchar.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/fputc.html#ERRORS/EBADF
anchor     functions/fputc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       On an unbuffered stdout whose descriptor 1 was closed, putchar()
           returns EOF, sets errno to EBADF and sets the error indicator of
           stdout.
note       Where setvbuf() refuses _IONBF (support for the buffering modes is
           implementation-defined, XSH 2.5), the test writes until a call
           fails, since a buffer that needs flushing brings the same error;
           if none does within 4 MiB the result is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/004-ebadf-closed.c

assertion  XSH.putchar.005
anchor     functions/putchar.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/fputc.html#ERRORS/EPIPE
anchor     functions/fputc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       With SIGPIPE blocked, on an unbuffered stdout that is the write
           end of a pipe whose read end is closed, putchar() returns EOF with
           errno EPIPE and the error indicator set, and SIGPIPE is then
           pending.
note       As XSH.putchar.004: where setvbuf() refuses _IONBF (support for
           the buffering modes is implementation-defined, XSH 2.5) the test
           writes until a call fails, and if none does within 4 MiB the
           result is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/005-epipe.c

assertion  XSH.putchar.006
anchor     functions/putchar.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/fputc.html#ERRORS/EAGAIN
anchor     functions/fputc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       With an unbuffered stdout that is the write end of a pipe filled
           to capacity with O_NONBLOCK set, putchar() returns EOF with errno
           EAGAIN and the error indicator set.
note       As XSH.putchar.004: where setvbuf() refuses _IONBF (support for
           the buffering modes is implementation-defined, XSH 2.5) the test
           writes until a call fails, and if none does within 4 MiB the
           result is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/006-eagain.c
